 ourselves as in opposition  the whole time we have to get in the  mindset of being in government if you're  in government this was what i said to my  shadow cabinet when we had the  discussion about the stripes if you're  in government and you're on the cabinet  table then you have to resolve these  issues you have to make sure that the  negotiations complete successfully mark  drakeford in wales did that he brought  the people together the parties together  and resolved the issue that's the role  of government before we stop i've got to  ask you this because we're at the  roundhouse in camden now lots of people  might not know this  you're quite a talented musician aren't  you uh well i was  like  what's the best gig you've ever been to  in the roundhouse  you're thinking i haven't been i haven't  been through oh orange juice i mean my  all-time favorite band played here  i don't i don't know orange juice  yeah  uh edward collins orange juice  rip it up  i don't know this is that they were here  but we went to see a deli other day with  the kids oh did she absolutely fantastic  yeah uh two or three weeks to see  coldplay you're going to see my wife's  absolute favorite now  so you coldplay adele  the other thing that people might  not know about you some things they  might not know you play football with  your friends once a week you take your  boy to arsenal matches and my girl now  well yeah and you get when you once your  daughter was younger you used to  pick her up from school  and used to organize your diary around i  don't think people might not know that  about you but this job your job is  totally encompassing you it can destroy  your marriage it can destroy your life  it can take over  did you ever harbour any ambiguity about  wanting to do this job  because of the impact on your family and  your family life that's the hardest bit  is the impact it has  um on my family it's the bit i worry  about the most it's why we never name  our children in public  it's why vic my wife doesn't do  interviews because  i want to protect them as best i can  because you know of course i'm in the  public eye that's the nature of the job  but it does take a toll on them we do  have some rules you know i try to ensure  that every friday by six o'clock i'm  home and i'm just there for vic and the  kids what did you do did you put your  phone in the bin or something well put  it in a job  but we do we get a takeaway on a friday  we have a family often fixed dad will  come over sometimes we do friday night  prayers with him um but um we then argue  about whether we're gonna watch  something on the television the kids  will be on their laptops  well vic's family is jewish  and so  her  dad  likes to have the friday night prayers  and um uh so we do that occasionally not  religiously everywhere you're not  religious yourself no but we want our  children to understand his jewish  um you know family  uh they came from poland we want them to  raise the children  no we don't but we want them to know  um that rick's family is jewish and to  know the traditions and the history to  understand you know what is part of  their family obviously now  one final question i've really run out  of time and everyone's sorry to wind up  um  tony blair gordon brown  um actually he's actually not gordon  brown but tony blair  and kinnick they they did you sort of  have their families more in the public  eye and you said it's a conscious  decision not but  you know when people sort of talk about  who is kirsten with a person  isn't your family like your biggest  asset in a way  yeah and vic is fantastic and everybody  who's seen or met vic says you know  she's fantastic and she is fantastic  absolutely fantastic  but i don't want you know we don't want  our family destroyed by all of this  of course it's a difficult one to get  right but  um you know i didn't we didn't have  children as sort of props in my  political life that's not why we had  kids we had kids because we wanted to  have a family of our own well kirsten i  should let you go because it's nearly  the weekend you've got to get home for  friday night thank you so much for  coming and talking to us on the show  today i appreciate it thanks for having  me thank you  and if you scan this qr code on your  screen now you can watch all of our  interviews online and all of the  previous episodes of the show
 

